        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Choose which A and which O",
        "body": "The word KANGAROO uses every point once: K, then an A, N, G, the other A, R, an O and finally the other O. The letters K, N, G, R appear once each, so the only freedom is\n- which of the two A's comes second (the other one is fifth): 2 ways,\n- which of the two O's comes seventh (the other one is eighth): 2 ways.\n\nEach choice gives a different broken line, so there are $2 \\cdot 2 = 4$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4**"
      }
    ],
