    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Football fans were travelling to a game in 32 minibuses. There was an equal number of people in each of them. Eight minibuses broke down on the way and the fans from these buses got on the remaining ones. After that there were two more fans in every minibus. How many fans were travelling to the game?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "48"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "144"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "192"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "256"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "384"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equation",
        "body": "With $n$ fans per bus: $32n = 24(n + 2)$, so $8n = 48$, $n = 6$ and there were $32 \\cdot 6 = 192$ fans.\n\n**Answer: (C) 192**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Redistribute",
        "body": "The fans of the 8 broken buses were spread over the 24 remaining buses, 2 per bus: that's $48$ fans, so each bus had $48 : 8 = 6$ fans. Total $32 \\cdot 6 = 192$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 192**"
      }
    ],
