    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "At which of the given times do the two hands of a watch form the smallest angle?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2:11"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "4:22"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "6:33"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "8:44"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "10:55"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angle formula",
        "body": "The minute hand moves $6^\\circ$ per minute, the hour hand $30^\\circ$ per hour plus $0.5^\\circ$ per minute. At $h{:}m$ the angle between them is $|30h + 0.5m - 6m| = |30h - 5.5m|$:\n- 2:11: $|60 - 60.5| = 0.5^\\circ$\n- 4:22: $|120 - 121| = 1^\\circ$\n- 6:33: $|180 - 181.5| = 1.5^\\circ$\n- 8:44: $|240 - 242| = 2^\\circ$\n- 10:55: $|300 - 302.5| = 2.5^\\circ$\n\nThe smallest angle is at 2:11.\n\n**Answer: (A) 2:11**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Time after the hands overlap",
        "body": "After $h$ o'clock the hands first overlap $\\frac{60h}{11}$ minutes later. Each listed time is $h$ o'clock plus $5.5h$ minutes, i.e. $5.5h - \\frac{60h}{11} = \\frac{h}{22}$ minutes after an overlap. The minute hand gains $5.5^\\circ$ per minute on the hour hand, so the angle is $5.5 \\cdot \\frac{h}{22} = \\frac h4$ degrees — smallest for $h = 2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 2:11**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "time-calendar",
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": "Official Canadian key gives (E) 10:55, but the angles are 0.5°, 1°, 1.5°, 2°, 2.5° for (A)-(E), so the smallest angle is at 2:11 (A). Answer set to (A); please check the key."
  },
