    "grade": "9-10",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The unit square is divided into a 9-square grid (fig. 1). Four line segments are drawn (fig. 2). What is the area of the shaded square?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2016-g0910/q28.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac13$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac25$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac{3\\sqrt2}{10}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac49$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Distance between parallel lines",
        "body": "Put the square at $(0,0)$–$(1,1)$. The segments join $(0,0)$ to $(\\frac13, 1)$, $(1,1)$ to $(\\frac23, 0)$, $(0,1)$ to $(1, \\frac23)$ and $(1,0)$ to $(0, \\frac13)$. The first two have direction $(1, 3)$, the last two direction $(3, -1)$ — perpendicular, so the shaded figure is indeed a rectangle, and its sides are the distances between the parallel lines.\n\nThe lines with direction $(1,3)$ through $(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$ are $3x - y = 0$ and $3x - y = 2$, at distance $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}$. The other two, $x + 3y = 3$ and $x + 3y = 1$, are also $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}$ apart. So the side of the square is $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}$ and the area is $\\frac{4}{10} = \\frac25$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac25$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
